ate":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:58:24-08:00","id":1193342,"title":"","content":"I wonder if this news undermines the classification of wolves and coyotes as separate species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:13:26-08:00","id":1193376,"title":"","content":"It's the Nuwisha's ultimate revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T13:22:59-08:00","id":1193683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1193376#post1193376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Nuwisha's ultimate revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T23:30:38-08:00","id":1193826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1193342#post1193342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if this news undermines the classification of wolves and coyotes as separate species.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, because species is far more complicated than &quot;can they make viable offspring&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T08:44:27-08:00","id":1193932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1193826#post1193826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, because species is far more complicated than &quot;can they make viable offspring&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>With American wolves, though, they have been a wolf/coyote/dog mix for a very long time. <a href=\"https://blogs.scientificamerican.com/guest-blog/the-hearty-ingredients-of-canis-soup/\" target=\"_blank\">This article</a> is a bit older, but it goes into the same direction as the OPs link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:57:20-08:00","id":1194054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1193932#post1193932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With American wolves, though, they have been a wolf/coyote/dog mix for a very long time. <a href=\"https://blogs.scientificamerican.com/guest-blog/the-hearty-ingredients-of-canis-soup/\" target=\"_blank\">This article</a> is a bit older, but it goes into the same direction as the OPs link.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which doesn't invalidate them as separate species. Species is a very complicated thing and a simple &quot;they can breed and make viable offspring&quot; is not the end all be all of why a two creatures are classified as the same species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T15:25:46-08:00","id":1194060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1194054#post1194054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which doesn't invalidate them as separate species. Species is a very complicated thing and a simple &quot;they can breed and make viable offspring&quot; is not the end all be all of why a two creatures are classified as the same species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, it is complicated. But as the article says, -what- these creatures are isn't that clear. Are eastern coyotes coyotes or wolves, for example.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that in game terms, nuwisha and garou function very differently. So where is the line that makes nuwisha nuwisha and garou garou, especially in mixed populations? Does dog blood dillute the shifter gene too much?<br /> <br /> Spiritually, as well, it might not be easy to figure which groups become which shifter. Eastern coyotes filled the ecological slot that wolves had in the area, so maybe they'd be garou rather than nuwisha. While red wolves might actually be nuwisha rather than garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T19:15:12-07:00","id":1199914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1194060#post1194060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, it is complicated. But as the article says, -what- these creatures are isn't that clear. Are eastern coyotes coyotes or wolves, for example.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that in game terms, nuwisha and garou function very differently. So where is the line that makes nuwisha nuwisha and garou garou, especially in mixed populations? Does dog blood dillute the shifter gene too much?<br /> <br /> Spiritually, as well, it might not be easy to figure which groups become which shifter. Eastern coyotes filled the ecological slot that wolves had in the area, so maybe they'd be garou rather than nuwisha. While red wolves might actually be nuwisha rather than garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my humble opinion, a red wolf could &quot;breed true&quot; into either Garou or Nuwisha, depending on what's in his or her ancestry. If Mama is a werewolf, the cub won't be Nuwisha, and if Mama is a werecoyote, the cub won't be Garou. If some ancestors have werewolf DNA and some ancestors have Nuwisha DNA, I guess it could go either way? The same question could come up for the &quot;Algonquin Wolf&quot; and the &quot;Mexican Wolf,&quot; which, like red wolves, may or may not be coywolves, depending on which biologist or conservationist you ask, but for the sake of the game, I don't think the dividing line between the species of canids matters so much as the spiritual nature of the fera in the cub's ancestry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","user":"Wilson","date":".  editing for clarity 03-26-2018, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T21:04:06-07:00","id":1199935,"title":"","content":"This raises the question of whether there can be mixed blood Nuwisha with Garou ancestry and genetics.<br /> <br /> The information presented about the coywolf implies that such a thing is possible.<br /> <br /> This leads one to wonder what such a creature would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T21:21:56-07:00","id":1199936,"title":"","content":"I imagine they'd be like how they describe Loki Nuwisha, more prone to violence than the rest of their kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:32:54-07:00","id":1200154,"title":"","content":"Somewhere, there's a Nuwisha laughing it's ass off","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T16:18:09-07:00","id":1200254,"title":"","content":"I would just give a Coywolf Nuwashi the Large merit and thats it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T01:21:39-07:00","id":1200735,"title":"","content":"Now I want to play a Nuwisha Garou hybrid...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T06:57:04-07:00","id":1200789,"title":"","content":"Calling it a hybrid seems to imply that it would somehow have access to both Breeds but it wouldn't. It would either by a Nuwisha or a Garou (with no pure breed) depending on the Mothers breed affinity, but it really wouldn't be both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T11:12:07-07:00","id":1200888,"title":"","content":"So at what pint does nonviable blood make a prospective child no longer a potential Garou? We know Garou can't breed with Dogs and expect Garou or Kinfolk. But would a 1/4th Dog be viable? And the domestication seems to be the only limiter for Garou so breeding with wild dogs or Coyotes would in theory not interfere right?<br /> <br /> Would be interesting if the Apocalypse happened the Tribes sacrificed themselves to save the Universe and new tribes formed, and one of them formed from Coywolfs and eventually became a Tribe of Coyote Garou, not Nuwisha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:55:50-07:00","id":1201257,"title":"","content":"I would be completely unsurprised if southern coywolves (aka C. rufus) had been Croatan kinfolk.<br /> <br /> And if I remember my Pure Land map correctly, northen coywolves stem from the confluence of Wendigo and Croatan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:58:16-07:00","id":1201259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1201257#post1201257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be completely unsurprised if southern coywolves (aka C. rufus) had been Croatan kinfolk.<br /> <br /> And if I remember my Pure Land map correctly, northen coywolves stem from the confluence of Wendigo and Croatan.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all likelyhood though those kinfolk would have been absorbed by the other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T17:26:44-07:00","id":1201479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1200888#post1200888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So at what pint does nonviable blood make a prospective child no longer a potential Garou? We know Garou can't breed with Dogs and expect Garou or Kinfolk. But would a 1/4th Dog be viable? And the domestication seems to be the only limiter for Garou so breeding with wild dogs or Coyotes would in theory not interfere right?<br /> <br /> Would be interesting if the Apocalypse happened the Tribes sacrificed themselves to save the Universe and new tribes formed, and one of them formed from Coywolfs and eventually became a Tribe of Coyote Garou, not Nuwisha.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Bunyip could get Garou from marsupials, surely there would be a way to get Garou from Eastern coyotes. It would probably take desperate conditions, such as post-apocalyptic survival, to get the Garou to willingly convert themselves into coyote-Garou, but I don't doubt it could be done. There's also the question of whether the Nuwisha would be amused or pissed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T17:32:45-07:00","id":1201481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1192928-coywolf?p=1201479#post1201479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Bunyip could get Garou from marsupials, surely there would be a way to get Garou from Eastern coyotes. It would probably take desperate conditions, such as post-apocalyptic survival, to get the Garou to willingly convert themselves into coyote-Garou, but I don't doubt it could be done. There's also the question of whether the Nuwisha would be amused or pissed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Bunyip needed special Magics from the Gumagan to breed with and become Thylacine. And Garou already can breed with Wild Canids like Dingos and Coyotes. I'm asking how many generations far from Domestic dogs before Garou blood becomes viable again. Because if Garou Breed with say a Golden Retriever their children won't be Garou or even Kinfolk. There is some sort of blunt Weaver taint that snuffs out the Gaian spirit nature of a shifter. So they can't breed with domestic animals, but if that half wolf half dog breeds with another full wolf/Garou would its kids finally be Kinfolk? Or do you have to go one more step of breeding?<br /> <br /> This makes me think of an idea I had for degenerate Bone Gnawers taking a bunch of dogs into Alaska or far northern Canada and start breeding with them to try to create a viable pool of wolf kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T15:21:05-07:00","id":1204988,"title":"","content":"There are also feral dogs to consider, where genetically domestic dogs live independently of any human care. These would most likely be urban strays, and their domestic breeding would yield domestic personalities regardless of human contact, but I wonder if they might take fewer generations to get back to &quot;wyld&quot; than, by contrast, a purebred German Shepherd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}